.TH SANCHALA-UPDATER 8 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sanchala-updater \- System update manager for Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-updater
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-updater
manages system updates with automatic snapshot creation, delta updates,
and safe rollback capabilities. It coordinates Pacman, Flatpak, and
firmware updates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Check for available updates
.TP
.B update \fR[\fB--security\fR|\fB--all\fR]
Apply updates (creates snapshot first)
.TP
.B schedule \fR[\fBenable\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
Manage automatic update schedule
.TP
.B history
Show update history
.TP
.B rollback \fR[\fISNAPSHOT\fR]
Rollback to previous state
.TP
.B changelog \fR[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
Show package changelogs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no-snapshot
Skip pre-update snapshot (not recommended)
.TP
.B \-\-download-only
Download updates without installing
.TP
.B \-\-reboot
Reboot after update if required
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check for updates:
.B sanchala-updater check
.TP
Apply security updates only:
.B sudo sanchala-updater update --security
.TP
Full system update:
.B sudo sanchala-updater update --all
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/updater/updater.toml
Configuration file
.TP
.I /var/lib/sanchala/updater/
Update state and history
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR sanchala-backup (1),
.BR snapper (8)
